# React coding style

## Files

- `.tsx` for JSX; `.ts` for hooks/types without JSX
- Tests: `.test.ts` / `.test.tsx` mirroring source

## Naming

- Components: `PascalCase` (`UserCard.tsx`)
- Hooks: `useCamelCase`
- Handlers: `handleClick` internally; props `onClick`
- Boolean props: `isLoading`, `hasError` — not bare `loading`

## Component shape

```tsx
type Props = {
  user: User
  onSelect: (id: string) => void
}

export function UserCard({ user, onSelect }: Props) {
  return (
    <button type="button" onClick={() => onSelect(user.id)}>
      {user.name}
    </button>
  )
}
```

- Destructure props in the parameter list
- No class components in new code
- Extract multi-line JSX logic to consts above `return`

## State

- Local first (`useState`), lift when shared
- TanStack Query for server-derived data — avoid `fetch` in `useEffect` when Query fits
- React Hook Form + Zod for complex forms (already in stack)

## Stack

TanStack Start + Vite — not Next.js App Router. No `"use client"` / RSC boundaries unless the file already uses them.

## Design tokens and chrome

Follow `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc` and `.cursor/skills/frontend-surfaces/SKILL.md` — read `design-system/MASTER.md` before UI work; do not invent colors, radius, or overlay patterns.
